WEBVTT

1
00:00:29.708 --> 00:00:31.916
<b>Here Krishna says</b>

2
00:00:31.916 --> 00:00:35.416
<b>that One who has renounced all desires</b>

3
00:00:35.416 --> 00:00:39.666
<b>and moves freely without any cravings,</b>

4
00:00:39.666 --> 00:00:42.916
<b>such a person has no ego,</b>

5
00:00:42.916 --> 00:00:45.666
<b>no sense of ownership,</b>

6
00:00:45.666 --> 00:00:47.041
<b>and only such a person</b>

7
00:00:47.041 --> 00:00:49.500
<b>attains peace.</b>

8
00:00:54.333 --> 00:00:55.208
<b>Here,</b>

9
00:00:55.208 --> 00:01:01.958
<b>Krishna mentions three characteristics </b>
<b>of a person with steady wisdom:</b>

10
00:01:01.958 --> 00:01:03.375
<b>Nihspruhah</b>

11
00:01:03.375 --> 00:01:06.250
<b>- Free from desires</b>

12
00:01:06.250 --> 00:01:07.166
<b>Nirmama</b>

13
00:01:07.166 --> 00:01:10.958
<b>- Free from the sense of ownership</b>

14
00:01:10.958 --> 00:01:12.416
<b>Nirankarah</b>

15
00:01:12.416 --> 00:01:16.416
<b>- Free from ego</b>

16
00:01:16.416 --> 00:01:19.166
<b>One who has attained these three qualities</b>

17
00:01:19.166 --> 00:01:24.000
<b>walks freely in this world with only one purpose</b>

18
00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:27.375
<b>- to understand their spiritual depth.</b>

19
00:01:27.375 --> 00:01:32.250
<b>Such a person remains content </b>
<b>with life's minimal necessities.</b>

20
00:01:32.250 --> 00:01:34.750
<b>They sustain themselves with just these</b>

21
00:01:34.750 --> 00:01:39.500
<b>and invest their energy solely </b>
<b>in spiritual pursuits.</b>

22
00:01:39.500 --> 00:01:45.666
<b>This certainly doesn't mean that such</b>
<b>a person has no worldly duties.</b>

23
00:01:45.666 --> 00:01:50.541
<b>They do. They fulfill their</b>
<b>responsibilities completely,</b>

24
00:01:50.541 --> 00:01:51.416
<b>but</b>

25
00:01:51.416 --> 00:01:55.875
<b>don't waste mental energy </b>
<b>worrying about outcomes.</b>

26
00:01:55.875 --> 00:01:59.416
<b>They simply perform their actions.</b>

27
00:01:59.416 --> 00:02:03.250
<b>If you contemplate this deeply, you'll understand</b>

28
00:02:03.250 --> 00:02:13.583
<b>that a person entangled in worldly attachments</b>
<b>typically lives only in the future or past.</b>

29
00:02:13.583 --> 00:02:14.833
<b>Either lamenting</b>

30
00:02:14.833 --> 00:02:16.125
<b>or thinking</b>

31
00:02:16.125 --> 00:02:20.666
<b>what has gone by. Or needlessly worrying </b>
<b>or thinking about what will come.</b>

32
00:02:20.666 --> 00:02:23.041
<b>But both are futile.</b>

33
00:02:23.041 --> 00:02:27.666
<b>A person of steady wisdom lives in the present.</b>

34
00:02:27.666 --> 00:02:29.333
<b>Performs their duties.</b>

35
00:02:29.333 --> 00:02:32.958
<b>And dedicates their time to spirituality.</b>

36
00:02:32.958 --> 00:02:35.791
<b>Whether circumstances are difficult or easy,</b>

37
00:02:35.791 --> 00:02:40.958
<b>such a person lives their life only in peace.</b>

38
00:02:40.958 --> 00:02:42.791
<b>The next verse</b>

39
00:02:42.791 --> 00:02:48.958
<b>will describe what they achieve in </b>
<b>their next birth after death.</b>

40
00:02:53.291 --> 00:02:55.458
<b>Ordinarily,</b>

41
00:02:55.458 --> 00:03:02.250
<b> humans help others only with some expectation.</b>

42
00:03:02.250 --> 00:03:06.333
<b>Either expecting praise, reward,</b>

43
00:03:06.333 --> 00:03:13.708
<b>or future returns and gratitude from others.</b>

44
00:03:13.708 --> 00:03:16.625
<b>A person surrounded only by expectations</b>

45
00:03:16.625 --> 00:03:23.833
<b>is deprived of such great wealth</b>
<b>of joy and happiness.</b>

46
00:03:23.833 --> 00:03:30.416
<b>If they help others selflessly, abandoning ego,</b>

47
00:03:30.416 --> 00:03:36.958
<b>then they'll know the supreme joy of true service.</b>

48
00:03:36.958 --> 00:03:47.125
<b>Service whose purpose is the welfare of others, </b>
<b>the betterment of society.</b>

49
00:03:47.125 --> 00:03:48.583
<b>A mother</b>

50
00:03:48.583 --> 00:03:52.875
<b>who nurtures her child without self-interest,</b>

51
00:03:52.875 --> 00:03:54.166
<b>a soldier</b>

52
00:03:54.166 --> 00:03:59.416
<b>who risks their life protecting the nation,</b>

53
00:03:59.416 --> 00:04:01.000
<b>a doctor</b>

54
00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:06.416
<b>who strives to heal others.</b>

55
00:04:06.416 --> 00:04:07.625
<b>Yes,</b>

56
00:04:07.625 --> 00:04:09.041
<b>undoubtedly</b>

57
00:04:09.041 --> 00:04:16.583
<b>some choose these professions</b>
<b>for livelihood, which is necessary,</b>

58
00:04:16.583 --> 00:04:17.791
<b>but</b>

59
00:04:17.791 --> 00:04:25.791
<b>one cannot deny that the core spirit of these </b>
<b>professions isn't self-interest or profit,</b>

60
00:04:25.791 --> 00:04:26.958
<b>but</b>

61
00:04:26.958 --> 00:04:30.208
<b>social welfare.</b>

62
00:04:30.208 --> 00:04:32.583
<b>Social welfare</b>

63
00:04:32.583 --> 00:04:35.708
<b>- that's my purpose too</b>

64
00:04:35.708 --> 00:04:39.875
<b>in participating in this great war of Mahabharata.</b>

65
00:04:39.875 --> 00:04:43.125
<b>In becoming Arjuna's charioteer.</b>

66
00:04:43.125 --> 00:04:46.291
<b>If profit were my motive,</b>

67
00:04:46.291 --> 00:04:50.458
<b>I wouldn't have given my army to Duryodhana.</b>

68
00:04:50.458 --> 00:04:54.375
<b>If fame and ego were my purpose,</b>

69
00:04:54.375 --> 00:04:58.500
<b>I would have fought as a warrior,</b>

70
00:04:58.500 --> 00:05:02.250
<b>not become Arjuna's charioteer.</b>

71
00:05:02.250 --> 00:05:05.833
<b>But my purpose is clear</b>

72
00:05:05.833 --> 00:05:10.291
<b>- dharma's victory over adharma.</b>

73
00:05:10.291 --> 00:05:11.541
<b>And</b>

74
00:05:11.541 --> 00:05:16.000
<b>the eternal welfare of all humanity.</b>

75
00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:20.666
<b>That's why I accepted this role,</b>

76
00:05:20.666 --> 00:05:21.958
<b>and now</b>

77
00:05:21.958 --> 00:05:25.458
<b>I guide Arjuna.</b>

78
00:05:25.458 --> 00:05:32.458
<b>Providing him with timeless wisdom </b>
<b>that will help not just him</b>

79
00:05:32.458 --> 00:05:33.583
<b>but</b>

80
00:05:33.583 --> 00:05:38.708
<b>everyone in times to come.</b>

81
00:05:38.708 --> 00:05:45.291
<b>That ocean of wisdom's small drop is before you – </b>

82
00:05:45.291 --> 00:05:51.208
<b>try helping someone selflessly,</b>

83
00:05:51.208 --> 00:05:56.500
<b>perform your duties without expecting returns.</b>

84
00:05:56.500 --> 00:06:00.958
<b>You'll experience boundless satisfaction.</b>

85
00:06:05.750 --> 00:06:06.750
<b>Family,</b>

86
00:06:06.750 --> 00:06:07.875
<b>community,</b>

87
00:06:07.875 --> 00:06:09.416
<b>this society –</b>

88
00:06:09.416 --> 00:06:13.375
<b>all stand on the strength of relationships.</b>

89
00:06:13.375 --> 00:06:19.125
<b>These relationships provide strength</b>
<b>to the family structure,</b>

90
00:06:19.125 --> 00:06:22.916
<b>becoming its source of energy.</b>

91
00:06:22.916 --> 00:06:23.958
<b>But</b>

92
00:06:23.958 --> 00:06:28.041
<b>when ego infests these relationships,</b>

93
00:06:28.041 --> 00:06:32.583
<b>their framework becomes hollow from within,</b>

94
00:06:32.583 --> 00:06:35.750
<b>starts breaking.</b>

95
00:06:35.750 --> 00:06:39.875
<b>Ego creates insecurity.</b>

96
00:06:39.875 --> 00:06:45.750
<b>One needlessly feels others will harm them,</b>

97
00:06:45.750 --> 00:06:48.708
<b>take away their rights.</b>

98
00:06:48.708 --> 00:06:58.791
<b>Then, seeking security, they begin hoarding </b>
<b>possessions, wealth, property,</b>

99
00:06:58.791 --> 00:07:01.875
<b>sharing with none.</b>

100
00:07:01.875 --> 00:07:06.083
<b>Insecurity has now taken the form of selfishness.</b>

101
00:07:06.083 --> 00:07:13.750
<b>For some time, such a person</b>
<b>feels power and security,</b>

102
00:07:13.750 --> 00:07:14.583
<b>but</b>

103
00:07:14.583 --> 00:07:21.416
<b>when their eyes open, they realize it's too late.</b>

104
00:07:21.416 --> 00:07:25.333
<b>They've pushed away all loved ones</b>

105
00:07:25.333 --> 00:07:33.416
<b>and now stand alone on </b>
<b>an island of ego and selfishness.</b>

106
00:07:33.416 --> 00:07:37.958
<b>Around them isn't the </b>
<b>sweet water of relationships,</b>

107
00:07:37.958 --> 00:07:43.083
<b>but only the salty water of solitude,</b>

108
00:07:43.083 --> 00:07:48.000
<b>which cannot quench a loveless mind's thirst.</b>

109
00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:51.166
<b>Ego will destroy relationships</b>

110
00:07:51.166 --> 00:07:53.416
<b>– avoid such ego.</b>

111
00:07:53.416 --> 00:07:57.375
<b>In relationships, don't think about who is right,</b>

112
00:07:57.375 --> 00:08:00.916
<b>think about what is right.</b>

113
00:08:00.916 --> 00:08:05.500
<b>Resolve major differences </b>
<b>through loving dialogue.</b>

114
00:08:05.500 --> 00:08:09.583
<b>And overlook minor ones.</b>

115
00:08:14.000 --> 00:08:17.208
<b>Ego makes much noise.</b>

116
00:08:17.208 --> 00:08:21.291
<b>I am supreme. Whatever was done, I alone did it.</b>

117
00:08:21.291 --> 00:08:25.208
<b>Without me, nothing would be right.</b>

118
00:08:25.208 --> 00:08:30.875
<b>Ego remains focused on I, and only I.</b>

119
00:08:30.875 --> 00:08:34.875
<b>Such a person never finds peace.</b>

120
00:08:34.875 --> 00:08:36.250
<b>Because</b>

121
00:08:36.250 --> 00:08:41.833
<b>another's progress creates insecurity in them.</b>

122
00:08:41.833 --> 00:08:44.208
<b>If someone else becomes better,</b>

123
00:08:44.208 --> 00:08:48.291
<b>then what happens to that "I".</b>

124
00:08:48.291 --> 00:08:53.625
<b>Consumed by such anxieties, one forgets</b>

125
00:08:53.625 --> 00:09:01.291
<b>that professional life's purpose</b>
<b>is to progress together.</b>

126
00:09:01.291 --> 00:09:07.750
<b>Some questions might arise here – </b>

127
00:09:07.750 --> 00:09:11.916
<b>Should we stop believing we're excellent?</b>

128
00:09:11.916 --> 00:09:15.833
<b>Should we not take credit for achievements?</b>

129
00:09:15.833 --> 00:09:22.541
<b>Here, know the difference between </b>
<b>ego and self-confidence.</b>

130
00:09:22.541 --> 00:09:24.083
<b>Self-confidence</b>

131
00:09:24.083 --> 00:09:25.666
<b>takes credit,</b>

132
00:09:25.666 --> 00:09:27.041
<b>but</b>

133
00:09:27.041 --> 00:09:29.416
<b>knows how to give it too.</b>

134
00:09:29.416 --> 00:09:32.708
<b>Self-confidence acknowledges its excellence,</b>

135
00:09:32.708 --> 00:09:33.625
<b>but</b>

136
00:09:33.625 --> 00:09:37.250
<b>doesn't underestimate others' capabilities.</b>

137
00:09:37.250 --> 00:09:42.916
<b>Self-confidence doesn't become </b>
<b>insecure when others advance,</b>

138
00:09:42.916 --> 00:09:49.500
<b>rather learns lessons from such </b>
<b>situations to progress further.</b>

139
00:09:49.500 --> 00:09:51.583
<b>For professional leadership,</b>

140
00:09:51.583 --> 00:09:58.333
<b>that person excels who is </b>
<b>self-confident but not egoistic.</b>

141
00:09:58.333 --> 00:10:01.416
<b>They give due credit to all.</b>

142
00:10:01.416 --> 00:10:04.625
<b>Respect others' existence.</b>

143
00:10:04.625 --> 00:10:06.333
<b>Consequently,</b>

144
00:10:06.333 --> 00:10:13.083
<b>people cooperate with them not </b>
<b>out of compulsion, but willingly.</b>

145
00:10:13.083 --> 00:10:18.208
<b>And if such a person feels </b>
<b>no insecurity from others,</b>

146
00:10:18.208 --> 00:10:21.083
<b>then what cause for unrest?</b>

147
00:10:21.083 --> 00:10:23.500
<b>Keep ambitions,</b>

148
00:10:23.500 --> 00:10:26.416
<b>but without ego.</b>

149
00:10:26.416 --> 00:10:28.250
<b>Keep progressing,</b>

150
00:10:28.250 --> 00:10:31.333
<b>with your self-confidence.</b>

